	(text "inSomnia — adaptive wake clock  |  ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8d8f8325-8a0e-4490-9d3a-571d9481dfef")
	)
	(text "RESERVED — DO NOT USE on N16R8: IO35 / IO36 / IO37 are wired to the\noctal PSRAM inside the module. IO0, IO3, IO45, IO46 are boot straps.\nIO46 is input-only. All are left as no-connect here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 128 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1d3e9e8d-fe76-4051-93c6-fd40bafd0cc2")
	)
	(text "KEYPAD — active LOW (10k pull-up per key, switch to GND).\nChain: U2.Q7 -> U3.DS, U3.Q7 -> SHIFT_DATA (U3 is read out first).\n74HC165 shifts D7 first, so the firmware bit order is:\n  bit0..7  = U3 D7..D0 = Key 1..8\n  bit8..11 = U2 D7..D4 = Key 9..12\nU2 D3..D0 tied to +3V3 (spare, always reads \"not pressed\")."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25 142 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "76e107a1-18ae-4c76-8020-d44552aae3eb")
	)
	(text "J5 = MLX90640 32x24 thermal array (I2C 0x33). It sits on the clock aimed\nat the bed and replaces BOTH the mattress accelerometer and the PIR:\nframe differencing gives contactless actigraphy, and a warm body-sized\nregion gives a direct in-bed / out-of-bed reading. No wire to the bed.\nOnly 4 of J5 five pins are used (VIN/GND/SDA/SCL).\nJ6 is now a spare 3-pin header on +5V / IO14 / GND.\nJ4 INMP441 L/R is tied to GND = LEFT channel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 160 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "85f3812d-488b-4b2a-a350-c6a125e779da")
	)
